==English==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|ear|piece}}.
[[Image:Headphones_Sony_super-light.jpg|thumb|An earpiece from a set of [[headphone]]s.]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɪəpiːs/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɪɹpiːs/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-earpiece.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[speaker]] placed inside or held near to the [[ear]].
#: {{hol|en|headpiece<qq:sometimes holonymous>}}
#: {{comeronyms|en|mouthpiece<qq:sometimes comeronymous>}}
#: {{cot|en|mouthpiece}}
#: {{ux|en|Holding the '''earpiece''' to my ear, I could hear him speaking clearly.}}
# A [[receiver]] of a telephone to hold near to one's ear.
# The arm on a [[pair of glasses]] that hooks over the [[ear]] to hold them in place.
#: {{ux|en|My glasses won't stay on, as I've broken the left '''earpiece'''.}}

